---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base title="DigiPets — Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for the DigiPets mobile app.">
  <Header currentPath="/privacy/digipets" />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[1280px] px-12 pt-36 pb-20 max-md:px-6 max-md:pt-20">
    <div data-i18n="pp_label" class="mb-7 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[2.5px] text-accent">
      Privacy Policy
    </div>
    <h1 data-i18n="pp_title" class="mb-6 max-w-[620px] text-[42px] font-light leading-tight tracking-tight max-md:text-3xl">
      DigiPets
    </h1>
    <div class="mb-12 text-sm text-text-3">
      <p data-i18n="pp_effective">Effective date: September 8, 2026</p>
      <a href="#data-deletion" data-i18n="pp_deletion_link" class="mt-3 inline-flex border-b border-accent/30 text-accent no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent">
        Request account and game data deletion
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-[600px] space-y-10">
      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_intro" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Introduction</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_intro" class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          DigiPets ("the App") is a free virtual pet game developed by David Luky ("we", "us"). This policy explains what data the App collects, how it is used, and your rights.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_collect" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          <li data-i18n="pp_c1">An anonymous user ID generated by Firebase Authentication. No email or legal name is required to use the App.</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_c2">Game progress data (pet stats, inventory, coins, achievements) stored in Cloud Firestore and associated with your anonymous ID.</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_c3">If you choose to sign in with Google, Firebase Authentication may receive your email address and basic profile information such as your display name or profile photo when Google includes them in the credential. If you link an email/password account, that email is stored securely by Firebase Authentication. The App uses the email address for account linking and does not use or display the Google profile photo or display name.</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_c4">If you use Friends, social data such as your shareable friend code, active pet name and summary, friendships, requests, visits, house summary, and kudos activity.</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_c5">Firebase may process a per-installation identifier (FID). Firebase App Check may also process Play Integrity app/device integrity signals to protect backend requests from abuse. This information is not used for advertising or user tracking.</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_c6">When you block or report a player, the App stores the account IDs involved. Safety reports also contain the selected reason, report status, and timestamps. We use this information to prevent abuse and review reports.</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_c7">If you enable Android push notifications, a Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) registration token associated with your account, selected locale, and last update time.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_not_collect" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          <li data-i18n="pp_nc1">Location data</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_nc2">Your device address book or phone number</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_nc3">Access to photos stored on your device, camera, or microphone</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_nc4">Advertising IDs or device identifiers used for advertising or tracking</li>
          <li data-i18n="pp_nc5">Third-party analytics, advertising tracking, or crash-reporting SDKs</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_use" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">How we use your data</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_use" class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          We use your data to save game progress, support optional Google sign-in and email/password account linking, and provide Friends, requests, and visits. We do not sell or monetize your data. Limited social profile details are shown through friend-code and accepted-friend flows; friend, request, and visit records are scoped to the involved accounts.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_notifications" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Notifications and push delivery</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_notifications" class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          Push notifications are optional on Android. If you enable them, Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) uses the registration token associated with your DigiPets account, selected locale, and last update time to deliver account and game notifications. The App also stores private inbox messages and whether you have read or dismissed them. Disabling push stops delivery to this installation. The App tries to remove the server registration when connected, and removes tokens reported invalid by Firebase during delivery attempts. Notification delivery is not used for marketing or notification analytics. The notification content shown on a device is generic and does not include a pet name. Device and installation identifiers described above remain used only for App functionality, not advertising or user tracking.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_thirdparty" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Third-party services</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_tp" data-i18n-html class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          The App uses <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" class="border-b border-accent/30 text-accent no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent">Google Firebase</a> for authentication, cloud data storage, and server-side game and social commands. Firebase's own privacy policy applies to data processed by its infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_children" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_children" class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          The App is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect their personal information. Anonymous play does not require an email or legal name. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="data-deletion" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_deletion" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Data deletion</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_deletion" data-i18n-html class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          To request account and game data deletion at any time, email <a href="mailto:davidluky@davidluky.com" class="border-b border-accent/30 text-accent no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent">davidluky@davidluky.com</a>. We will delete your account and all associated game data within 30 days. Block records associated with your account are included in that deletion. Safety reports are scheduled for automatic deletion 30 days after they are created.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_changes" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_changes" class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 data-i18n="pp_h_contact" class="mb-3 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text">Contact</h2>
        <p data-i18n="pp_contact" data-i18n-html class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-text-2">
          Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:davidluky@davidluky.com" class="border-b border-accent/30 text-accent no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent">davidluky@davidluky.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<script>
